--- promikailamin ---
Implemented the BadVillager feature and pushed it to `main` (commit `415c22d`).

Changes:
- Villagers standing on a redstone block instantly become `BadVillager` (dark-red bold name tag).
- While tagged `BadVillager`, the villager is invincible to all damage sources.
- Any attacker that hits a BadVillager receives a random-level Bad Omen effect for 20 minutes.
- Stepping off the redstone block removes the tag, name, and invincibility.
- The CreateVillager iron-block check now also runs every tick instead of every 10 seconds.
- Updated README and rebuilt the distribution/test-server JAR.

Validation:
- `./gradlew build` completed successfully.
- Started a 26.2 server and verified: BadVillager tag/name applied instantly, damage blocked (health unchanged), attacker received `minecraft:bad_omen`, and after teleporting off the redstone block the tag disappeared and the villager took normal damage. CreateVillager conversion also still works instantly.
